  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a polynomial of degree <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;in which the coefficient of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math> is unity and it has extrema at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "144",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi></math><p>as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;non-zero finite</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Solving both we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn></math></p>",
